@host = http://localhost:5187

# Story 18 - the ticket conversation thread: agent replies, customer replies, internal notes, the history (Story 15 activities)
# and the cursor-paged thread. Run top to bottom against a Development API (`docker compose up -d`, then
# `dotnet run --project backend/src/Crm.Api --launch-profile http`). The file creates its own tickets, so it runs on any
# database state. rowVersion is needed only for the status transitions; `@after` values chain from the previous response.
# Access tokens live 2 minutes in Development - re-run the logins when a request answers 401. Sign-in is limited to 30/min.
# Every entry of the thread has a per-ticket `sequence` (Ticket.Revision at append); the thread is ordered by it and paged with
# `after={last sequence}`. Visibility: public = messages, internal = notes, system = activities (history).
# Requests 37/38 read their body from ./data/*.json (`<` file reference of the VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client).
# Dev seed: T-000001 Ahmed (RYD-CARE, New), T-000003 Red Sea (JED-CARE, New - invisible to agent A).

@ahmed = 11000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@ahmedContact = 11000000-0000-0000-0001-000000000001
@agentA = 06000000-0000-0000-0003-000000000003
@ahmedNewTicket = 15000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@redSeaNewTicket = 15000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@unknown = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000dead

### Login as agent A (Agent in RYD-CARE)
# @name loginAgentA
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.a@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@agentAToken = {{loginAgentA.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login as agent B (Agent in JED-CARE)
# @name loginAgentB
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.b@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@agentBToken = {{loginAgentB.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login as supervisor (Supervisor in RYD-CARE)
# @name loginSupervisor
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "supervisor@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@supervisorToken = {{loginSupervisor.response.body.accessToken}}

###############################################################################################################################
### Setup and the first entries
###############################################################################################################################

### 1. Create a ticket for Ahmed - 200 (@th): allowedActions contains Reply and AddNote
# @name th
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{
  "customerId": "{{ahmed}}",
  "contactId": "{{ahmedContact}}",
  "subject": "Conversation test",
  "description": "A ticket that exercises the conversation thread."
}

@thId = {{th.response.body.id}}

### 2. The thread of the new ticket - 200: one item { sequence 1, type Activity, visibility System, templateKey Created,
### parameters { from: null, to: New } }, nextCursor null, people names agent A
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 3. Agent reply - 200; status New; firstRespondedAtUtc set. EF log: split SELECTs over TicketActivities/TicketMessages/TicketNotes,
### INSERT INTO [tickets].[TicketMessages], UPDATE [tickets].[Tickets] ... [Revision] ... AND [RowVersion] = @..., one outbox INSERT
# @name r3
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "  Hello Ahmed,\nwe are looking into it.  " }

### 4. Entries after sequence 1 - 200: exactly one item, sequence 2, type Message, direction Outbound, body "Hello Ahmed,\nwe are
### looking into it." (trimmed, line break kept), authorId = recordedById = agent A
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?after=1
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 5. Second reply - 200; firstRespondedAtUtc EQUAL to request 3's (only the first agent reply sets it)
# @name r5
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Second reply" }

### 6. Internal note - 200; status unchanged. EF log: INSERT INTO [tickets].[TicketNotes]; no outbox INSERT
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Internal: customer is on the VIP list." }

### 7. Note with markup - 200: stored verbatim (plain text, never parsed or rendered as HTML)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "<b>not bold</b> <script>alert(1)</script>" }

### 8. Arabic reply - 200
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "شكراً لتواصلك معنا.\nسنعود إليك قريباً." }

###############################################################################################################################
### Reading the thread: visibility and paging
###############################################################################################################################

### 9. The whole thread - 200: sequences 1..6 ascending - Activity, Message, Message, Note, Note, Message; notes have visibility Internal
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 10. Internal only - 200: the two notes
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?visibility=internal
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 11. Public only - 200: the three messages, NO Note entry. EF log: no [TicketNotes] and no [TicketActivities] SQL
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?visibility=public
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 12. System and public - 200: Created + the three messages
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?visibility=system&visibility=public
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 13. First page of two - 200: sequences 1, 2; nextCursor 2
# @name page1
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 14. A note is added while paging - 200 (sequence 7)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Added while paging" }

### 15. Second page - 200: sequences 3, 4; nextCursor 4
# @name page2
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?limit=2&after={{page1.response.body.nextCursor}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 16. Third page - 200: sequences 5, 6, 7 (the note from 14 last), nextCursor null. Pages 13 + 15 + 16 hold 1..7 exactly once
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?limit=10&after={{page2.response.body.nextCursor}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

###############################################################################################################################
### Status rules
###############################################################################################################################

### 17. The ticket - 200: activities = one Created; rowVersion for request 18
# @name th1
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 17b. Open the ticket - 200 Open (appends the Opened activity as sequence 8; AwaitCustomer is not allowed from New)
# @name th1o
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "Open", "rowVersion": "{{th1.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 18. Await the customer - 200 PendingCustomer (appends the AwaitingCustomer activity as sequence 9)
# @name th2
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "AwaitCustomer", "rowVersion": "{{th1o.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 19. Customer reply on PendingCustomer - 200; status Open. Two outbox INSERTs (message + status)
# @name r19
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/customer-replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Here is the screenshot you asked for." }

### 20. Reply on a SEEDED ticket - 200: the back-filled sequences of the Story 15 rows accept a new entry
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{ahmedNewTicket}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Reply on a seeded ticket." }

### 21. Entries after sequence 9 - 200: sequence 10 Message Inbound (authorId = Ahmed contact, recordedById = agent A); sequence 11
### Activity Opened { from: PendingCustomer, to: Open }
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?after=9
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 22. Customer reply on an Open ticket - 200; status stays Open; exactly one new entry (sequence 12)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/customer-replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Any update?" }

### 22b. Entries after sequence 11 - 200: exactly one entry, sequence 12
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?after=11
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 23a. The ticket (fresh rowVersion) - 200
# @name th3
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 23b. Resolve - 200 Resolved (sequence 13)
# @name th4
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "Resolve", "rowVersion": "{{th3.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 24. allowedActions of the Resolved ticket - contains Reply, AddNote, Close, Reopen
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 25. Reply to a Resolved ticket - 200; status Open, resolvedAtUtc null. Entries after 13: Message 14, Activity Reopened 15
### { from: Resolved, to: Open }. Two outbox INSERTs (message + status changed)
# @name r25
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "One more detail before we close." }

### 25b. Entries after 13 - 200: Message 14 then Activity Reopened 15
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/thread?after=13
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 26a. Resolve again (fresh rowVersion first)
# @name th5
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 26b. Resolve - 200 Resolved
# @name th6
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "Resolve", "rowVersion": "{{th5.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 26c. Customer reply on Resolved - 200; status Open via a Reopened activity
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/customer-replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "It works now, thanks!" }

### 27a. Fresh rowVersion
# @name th7
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 27b. Resolve - 200
# @name th8
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "Resolve", "rowVersion": "{{th7.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 27c. Close - 200 Closed; allowedActions has AddNote and Reopen, NOT Reply
# @name th9
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "Close", "rowVersion": "{{th8.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 28a. Reply to a Closed ticket (en) - 422 urn:crm:problem:domain-rule, code Tickets.TransitionNotAllowed,
### detail "The ticket is Closed; that action is not allowed in this status."
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}
Accept-Language: en

{ "body": "Too late" }

### 28b. Same in Arabic - 422, detail names the status «مغلقة»
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}
Accept-Language: ar

{ "body": "Too late" }

### 29. Customer reply on a Closed ticket - 422 Tickets.TransitionNotAllowed
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/customer-replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Hello?" }

### 30. Internal note on a Closed ticket - 200 (notes are allowed in every status)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Post-mortem note on a closed ticket." }

### 31a. Fresh rowVersion
# @name th10
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 31b. Reopen - 200 Open
# @name th11
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "Reopen", "rowVersion": "{{th10.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 31c. Await the customer - 200 PendingCustomer
# @name th12
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "AwaitCustomer", "rowVersion": "{{th11.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 31d. Customer reply - 200 Open; two outbox INSERTs (message + status changed)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{thId}}/customer-replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Back again." }

### 32a. A second ticket, cancelled (@th5Ticket) - 200
# @name th5Ticket
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{
  "customerId": "{{ahmed}}",
  "subject": "Cancelled conversation test",
  "description": "A ticket that is cancelled to prove replies are refused."
}

@th5Id = {{th5Ticket.response.body.id}}

### 32b. Cancel it - 200
# @name th5Cancelled
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{th5Id}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "Cancel", "rowVersion": "{{th5Ticket.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 32c. Reply to a Cancelled ticket - 422 Tickets.TransitionNotAllowed
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{th5Id}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Reply on a cancelled ticket" }

### 32d. Note on a Cancelled ticket - 200
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{th5Id}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "Note on a cancelled ticket" }

###############################################################################################################################
